  "note": "A Bde two Bns up with a depth Bn withdrawing by night (OOW3 2006 s2-s12; IBB s72-76 for each Bn). The click is the Bde HQ of the old posn; the aim is the way of withdrawal, the second click the new defensive posn (planned). Laid on OOW3 Annex P (p 75): rear parties left by each forward Bn (s9 para 5 p 45); the Bns back on their own axes to the clear line, several axes to avoid congestion and the En air, the routes converging from the outer flanks protected (s2 para 5 a p 8); covering troops delaying in front of each intermediate posn (s6 paras 9-13 pp 31-32); a flank guard on the threatened flank if required (para 24 p 34); two intermediate posns, each held by a complete unit under one Comd with more fire in front and less depth (paras 16-22 pp 33-34), each far enough beyond the one before that the En must re-deploy the field artillery (p 33; IBB p 373: the En 105 mm IFG 17.2 km, ORBAT); the depth Bn the reserve (s7 para 5 p 40); the primary demolition belt continuous across the new posn's front (s12 para 5 a p 56); the BL close to own troops and moved back often (p 67). More than one passage lane and a contact point at each posn passed through: Int Posn 1 and 2 and the new posn, through which the covering troops come back last (s10 paras 1-3 pp 47-50; Annex P). Timings in the Annex A pattern (pp 72-73). Posns are drawn turned to face the En behind the plan.",
